Z||000020||FieroGT||06-07-2000||08:51 AM||||There has got to be some available Fiero ladies out there, just that I never seem to find any. A friend of mine had a Fiero-girl about 5 years ago, he used to help her with her car a lot. I don't think that she really appreciated the white '85 L4 she drove. Oh, well....<p>[This message has been edited by FieroGT (edited 06-07-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000021||DaRkLoRD||06-07-2000||03:42 PM||||A girl I used to know became a Fiero girl when she was given a silver 86 GT for her 16th birthday... she didn't even know what it was, except it was a silver car that her dad used to race..... I'm not sure what mods it had, cause she didn't know.. heh.<P>last I heard she was dating some guy from scotland, over the net.. that was almost 2 years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000022||mrfixit58||06-08-2000||10:50 AM||||Someone always seems to wind up shot in relationships like these!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>One the other hand... she wants to go to a "strip club" with you?? Kinky!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Spyder||06-08-2000||10:51 AM||||The age thing is no big deal unless you were 18, lol.<BR>I am 29 and my wife is 24, and we are perfect together.<P>JUST HAVE FUN! Live Life and the rest will fall into place.<P>Early in a relationship:<BR>Listen to what she says<BR>This is a must: Don’t get mushy and tell her your real feelings (save this for later)<BR>Don’t talk about your X.<BR>Don’t complain about anything.<BR>Smile a lot.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||FieroGT||06-08-2000||01:31 PM||||Spyder,<P>Sounds like good advice. I always like to keep myself a bit mysterious, but I already talked about my ex to her, maybe indirectly, since she was always around my circle of friends (ranging from 23 to 38 yrs. old). I've heard all of her ex stories, as well, and one nice thing is that we both completely accept the past without dwelling on it and have nothing to hide from each other. Actually, got a date on Friday night! Damn, it's been a while, hope I still remember how to behave myself on these things......<P><BR>John||||reg||14
Z||000025||tgowens||06-08-2000||02:13 PM||||John, define "behave" !!!!!! -- good luck to ya and just enjoy each other's company and let things go where they may - but, above all - COMMUNICATE with each other -- this is the biggest reason a relationship will fail, one partner does not communicate thoughts, feelings, desires, wishes.............have a great time and be sure and tell her hello from all of us and let her know we are behind you both all the way (now that'll keep her turning around and looking over her shoulder all night!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000026||dogtired||06-09-2000||04:16 AM||||Sounds like she might be a KEEPER but proceed with CAUTION.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just re-read your first post and you say she likes your Fiero more than you???   Think about that!   She might just be after your car???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Just funnin a little <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. There are all types out there, I have had my current wife just over 30 years and I think she is a keeper. Guess one of these days I will figure out if I need to replace her? Guess she could turn it around and replace me??? It is turly a two way street. Hang in there.||||reg||6
Z||000027||FieroGT||06-09-2000||09:52 AM||||dogtired, what I meant is that she seems to like the car more than I do, not more than she likes me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Actually, her real passion is to go riding on the bike with me. She actually asks me to bring the bike with me when I come up to see her!<P>Actually, the Fiero sees about 4,000 a year now. I have a Saturn coupe I use for daily driving purposes, so I guess that she likes to ride in it, since it it such an intimate environment. At least she doesn't ask to drive it because she is not versed in the art of the manual trans! Might be a good thing....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>She called me last night and asked if I would like to go see "Gone in 60 Seconds". I'm still wondering if this is for real!!! Might just have to get her a tool set of her own! <P>John<BR>Founding member of CGWDNCWI<BR>(Car Guys Who Don't Need Chick With Issues)||||reg||14
